summary.novel_idea:
This work establishes the nuclear impulse approximation framework for sequential CC $
u_	au$/$ ar{
u}_	au$ hyperon/charmed-baryon production ($
u_	au n 	o 	au^- \Lambda_c^+$ and $ ar{
u}_	au p 	o 	au^+ \Lambda$) and subsequent $	au 	o \pi 
u_	au$ decay on nuclear targets ($^{16}\mathrm{O}$). It demonstrates that an event-by-event pion azimuthal asymmetry with respect to the reaction plane survives nuclear Fermi motion smearing as a clean, CP-odd observable that vanishes identically in the Standard Model.
